RIGHTS, PUBLIC-DOMAIN, AND CC0 NOTICE
=====================================

Historical source work
----------------------
Évariste Galois, Oeuvres mathematiques (Paris: Gauthier-Villars et fils,
1897), including the historical editorial matter and Emile Picard's
Introduction, is public-domain source material. Public-domain status is a
rights status, not a new license granted by this repository.

The source scans, catalogue records, manuscript witnesses, and other third-
party artifacts are identified separately in SOURCE_AUTHORITY.json and the
release provenance archive. This repository does not claim ownership of those
materials and does not alter whatever rights or use conditions apply to them.

Modern English translation and project contributions
----------------------------------------------------
To the extent the Manuscript Typesetting Project owns copyright or related
rights in the modern English translation, critical apparatus, modern
typesetting, metadata, build scripts, alignment and coverage records, and QA
evidence produced for this edition, it dedicates those contributions to the
public domain under Creative Commons CC0 1.0 Universal.

CC0 summary and legal code:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode

The translation and critical work were generated and checked with the model
roles disclosed in README.md and CITATION.cff. Those model names are production
attribution; they are not a claim that a model is a natural-person author,
translator, or rightsholder.

Limits
------
This dedication applies only to rights the project can lawfully waive. It does
not reassign historical authorship, extinguish moral rights where they cannot
be waived, or relicense third-party scans, catalogue metadata, fonts, software
dependencies, or witness material. Each bundled artifact retains the rights
status recorded in its own provenance entry.

